This feels like we're going back to the past again with CMU's Sphinx4 in Java. It worked way better than I would ever have expected it to for being more than a decade old. It relied on the user defining a grammar of valid words and different flows through a standard format (Java Speech API Grammar Format). I wonder if we'll approach that again for these models just like how MCPs act like WSDLs in spirit. Great results getting whistle working so well for you!  #JSGF V1.0;
  grammar commands;

  public <action> = open | close | delete ;
  public <object> = file | window | application ;
  public <command> = <action> [the] <object>;reply
